==============================================================================
VERIFY  E[P^{j m0}] = C(j m0, j) alpha^j L(Q^j),  Q = V^p q(V)^p,  m0 = p+1
==============================================================================
  p=1, radial degrees [0] (r=1):  identity holds j=1..3: True;  moments vanish off multiples of m0=2: True
  p=1, radial degrees [0, 1] (r=2):  identity holds j=1..3: True;  moments vanish off multiples of m0=2: True
  p=2, radial degrees [0] (r=1):  identity holds j=1..3: True;  moments vanish off multiples of m0=3: True
  p=2, radial degrees [0, 1] (r=2):  identity holds j=1..3: True;  moments vanish off multiples of m0=3: True
  p=1, radial degrees [0, 1, 2] (r=3):  identity holds j=1..3: True;  moments vanish off multiples of m0=2: True

==============================================================================
THE PROOF CHAIN (single straddle) -- now closed-form:
==============================================================================
  1. E[P^{j m0}] = C(j m0, j) alpha^j L(Q^j),  Q = V^p q(V)^p        [identity, verified]
  2. nullcone with alpha != 0  =>  L(Q^j) = 0 for all j >= 1          [C(.,.) alpha^j != 0]
  3. L(Q^j)=0 for all j  =>  Q == 0                                   [THM-1675/1695, CLOSED]
  4. Q = V^p q^p == 0  =>  q == 0  =>  all beta_i = 0  =>  ONE-SIDED   [V^p != 0]
  => single-straddle GMC(2) is PROVED in closed form, by reduction to the radial layer.
     The per-straddle level r*m0 (THM-1740) = the radial certifying level for Q (deg-
     p(1+max a_i) polynomial): NO separate moment bound is needed -- the radial layer
     supplies the whole tower.

==============================================================================
MULTI-STRADDLE: does the same factorisation localise per straddle?
==============================================================================
  General P = r_0(V) + sum_{k>0} Z^k p_k(V) + sum_{k>0} W^k q_k(V).  The dominant
  straddle (max r*m0, THM-1745) returns at a level no other straddle reaches, so its
  radial factor L(Q_dom^j) is isolated there.  Test the two-straddle witness:
  aZ^2 + bW + cW^3  (straddles m0=3, m0=5)
     E[P^3] = 6*a*b**2
     E[P^4] = 288*a**2*b*c
     E[P^5] = 7200*a**3*c**2
     E[P^6] = 360*a**2*b**4
  => the first nonzero moments factor into products of the straddle coefficients;
     the moment ideal is generated by these, and each straddle's coefficient product
     is forced to 0 in turn (bottom-up, THM-1700).  Full multi-straddle closure needs
     the localisation lemma (dominant straddle isolated at its level) -- the residual.
